 ## Background
-The concept of combining photometric losses with visibility weighting emerged in the context of differentiable rendering and neural radiance fields (NeRF) [S5]. Early works used simple L1 or L2 losses [S2]. The explicit incorporation of visibility maps to weight these losses was introduced to handle scenes with complex backgrounds or partial observations [S5]. Silhouette losses were added to enforce silhouette consistency [S4]. Shadow regularization was introduced in outdoor relighting contexts to prevent the shadow network from absorbing lighting information [S1].
+The concept of combining photometric losses with visibility weighting emerged in the context of differentiable rendering and neural radiance fields (NeRF) [S6]. Early works used simple L1 or L2 losses [S2]. The explicit incorporation of visibility maps to weight these losses was introduced to handle scenes with complex backgrounds or partial observations [S6]. Silhouette losses were added to enforce silhouette consistency [S4]. Shadow regularization was introduced in outdoor relighting contexts to prevent the shadow network from absorbing lighting information [S1].
 
